>> title: Batata Harra
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: potato, lebanese, deep-fry, cilantro, chiles
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: batata harra, batata harrah, batata hara, spicy potatoes, Lebanese spicy potatoes, potato cilantro, harra potatoes
>> pairs-with: toum, pita-bread, hummus
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> washing-up: the frying pot, a pot to parboil in, a colander, a rack to drain on, the mortar

>> step: parboil 6 min, then dry them out
Parboil @russet potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; peeled, in 3/4-in cubes) in heavily salted water ~simmer{6%min}, until a knife meets slight resistance, then drain and leave them ~dry{10%min} until the surfaces go chalky.

>> step: fry at 375°F 5 min until brittle
Fry @&(~1)parboiled potatoes{} in @neutral oil{4%cups}(950 mL; at 375°F/190°C) in two batches ~fry{5%min}, until they are dark gold and rattle against the spider, then drain them on a rack.

>> step: pound the garlic, cilantro and chile
Pound @garlic{6%cloves}, @cilantro{1%cup}(chopped, stems included), @red chile flakes{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{1%tsp} to a rough green paste in a #mortar{} with @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL).

>> step: toss off the heat
Toss @&(~2)fried potatoes{} with @&(~1)garlic paste{} and @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in the pan **off the heat**, until every cube is coated.
